Write a positive integer in each box (of the figure) so that:
the six numbers are distinct;
the sum of the six numbers is $100$;
if each number is multiplied by its neighbour (in the clockwise direction) and the six results of these six multiplications are added, the least possible value is obtained.
Explain why a smaller value cannot be obtained.

